push([1,\"ng-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Remember — at BestAnimalNames.com, we're here to help every step of the way. Our tools are 100% free, updated regularly, and designed to make pet naming joyful rather than stressful. Browse, explore, and discover the name that's been waiting for your special companion.\\\"]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"4e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How long should I wait before naming my new pet?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Most experts recommend waiting 2-5 days after bringing your pet home. This observation period lets you understand their personality, habits, and quirks before committing to a name. The name that feels right after a few days of bonding is usually the best choice.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can I rename an adopted or rescue pet?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Absolutely! Adult pets can learn new names with patience and positive reinforcement. Use lots of treats, enthusiastic praise, and consistent repetition. Most pets adjust to a new name within 2-4 weeks. The key is always associating the new name with positive experiences.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Should my pet's name match their breed heritage?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"It's a personal choice with no right or wrong answer. Breed-heritage names (like 'Angus' for a Scottish Terrier or 'Sakura' for a Shiba Inu) add cultural meaning, but countless pets thrive with names that have no connection to their breed origins. Choose what resonates with you.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What if my family can't agree on a name?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Create a democratic process: each person nominates their top three names, create a combined shortlist, and vote. You can also try a tournament bracket where names compete head-to-head until a champion emerges. The key is giving everyone a voice while keeping the process fun.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Are two-word names practical?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Two-word names like 'Luna Mae' or 'Buddy Boo' can work beautifully, especially if you primarily use the first word for everyday 